<title>GERMANY: Thyssen Handelsunion 95/96 profit plummets.</title>
<headline>Thyssen Handelsunion 95/96 profit plummets.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Sept 30 (In millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group pretax profit		   1.2     vs 227.0</p>
<p>    Group income from ord. activities 42.4    vs 227.0</p>
<p>    Extraordinary expenditures	  41.2    vs nil</p>
<p>    Group external sales		  18,180  vs 18,265</p>
<p>    Total business volume		 20,186  vs 20,021</p>
<p>    Cash flow				 370.6   vs 624.9</p>
<p>    Rohertrag				 3,567.3 vs 3,703.3</p>
<p>    Investments			     941.4   vs 937.9</p>
<p>    Depreciation			    371.8   vs 326.9</p>
<p>    Balance sheet total		   7,668.4 vs 7,692.6</p>
<p>    Capital assets			  2,488.1 vs 2,052.9</p>
<p>    Capital				   1,760.1 vs 1,534.2</p>
<p>    Workforce				 31,658  vs 31,791</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the trade and services unit of the Thyssen AG is Thyssen Handelsunion AG</p>
